L0237: Negation of an unsigned machine integer

Unary minus is not defined for unsigned machine values. Use a signed runtime type if the result must be executable, or observe the value as logical Int before mathematical negation in a logical expression.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/negate_unsigned.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```rust
// Unary minus exists at the signed types only, as in Rust.
fn negate(a: u8) -> u8 {
    -a
}

fn negate_wide(a: u64) -> u64 {
    -a
}
```

Language, as built: [1.3:1](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.3:1).
